      en: "Saint George Maronite Cathedral is a historic church in the heart of Beirut, standing directly adjacent to the grand Mohammad Al-Amin Mosque and symbolizing Lebanon's religious diversity. Built in the late 19th century in a Neoclassical style, the cathedral's design was inspired by the Basilica of Santa Maria Maggiore in Rome. Following extensive damage during the civil war, the magnificent structure was painstakingly restored and enhanced with a new, soaring bell tower."
