      en: "The Roman Baths of Beirut are a fascinating archaeological site located in the heart of the modern downtown, rediscovered only in 1968. The complex still displays the well-preserved brick pillars of the hypocaust, the ancient underfloor heating system that once warmed the hot rooms of the thermae. Today, the area is landscaped as an archaeological park and is frequently used as a picturesque venue for open-air concerts and cultural events."
